     "(This is mostly for Daniel.)<p>I&#39;m trying to track down the problem<br>with the normal unit test when we don&#39;t<br>clear the stack.<p>What I came across is that the tests<br>are generating new auto-dif variables<br>on the stack.<p>W/O TESTS:<p>STACK, size=13<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : 0<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 0<br>4  0x100800060  -4.6 : 0<br>5  0x100800088  21.16 : 0<br>6  0x1008000b0  10.89 : 0<br>7  0x1008000d8  21.78 : 0<br>8  0x100800100  0.971534 : 0<br>9  0x100800128  -0.971534 : 0<br>10  0x100800150  1.19392 : 0<br>11  0x100800170  -2.16546 : 0<br>12  0x100800198  -3.08439 : 0<p><br>WITH TESTS:<p>START STACK<br>STACK, size=20<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : 0<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 0<br>----------- due to testing ----<br>4  0x100800060  1.79769e+308 : 0<br>5  0x100800078  -1.79769e+308 : 0<br>6  0x100800098  1.79769e+308 : 0<br>7  0x1008000b0  1.79769e+308 : 0<br>8  0x1008000c8  -1.79769e+308 : 0<br>9  0x1008000e8  1.79769e+308 : 0<br>10  0x100800100  inf : 0<br>------------- ouch -----------------<br>11  0x100800118  -4.6 : 0<br>12  0x100800140  21.16 : 0<br>13  0x100800168  10.89 : 0<br>14  0x100800190  21.78 : 0<br>15  0x1008001b8  0.971534 : 0<br>16  0x1008001e0  -0.971534 : 0<br>17  0x100800208  1.19392 : 0<br>18  0x100800228  -2.16546 : 0<br>19  0x100800250  -3.08439 : 0<p>The extra variables are +/- min value<br>and infinity.  So perhaps just those<br>tests could be fixed by taking value<br>before passing in.<p>Note also there&#39;s no extra variables on<br>the stack.  So I&#39;m recovering memory.<br>But whether or not I run the first test<br>makes a difference.  Without the first<br>test, I get the right answer:<p>FAILED (INCLUDES FIRST GTEST)<br>--------------------------------<br>START STACK<br>STACK, size=13<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : 0<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 0<br>4  0x100800060  -4.6 : 0<br>5  0x100800088  21.16 : 0<br>6  0x1008000b0  10.89 : 0<br>7  0x1008000d8  21.78 : 0<br>8  0x100800100  0.971534 : 0<br>9  0x100800128  -0.971534 : 0<br>10  0x100800150  1.19392 : 0<br>11  0x100800170  -2.16546 : 0<br>12  0x100800198  -3.08439 : 0<p>MIDDLE STACK<br>STACK, size=13<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0.844812<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : -0.844812<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0.571556<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 2<br>4  0x100800060  -4.6 : 0.844812<br>5  0x100800088  21.16 : -0.0918274<br>6  0x1008000b0  10.89 : 0.178427<br>7  0x1008000d8  21.78 : 0.0892134<br>8  0x100800100  0.971534 : -2<br>9  0x100800128  -0.971534 : 2<br>10  0x100800150  1.19392 : -2<br>11  0x100800170  -2.16546 : 2<br>12  0x100800198  -3.08439 : 1<p>SUCCESS (NO FIRST GTEST)<br>------------------------<br>START STACK<br>STACK, size=13<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : 0<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 0<br>4  0x100800060  -4.6 : 0<br>5  0x100800088  21.16 : 0<br>6  0x1008000b0  10.89 : 0<br>7  0x1008000d8  21.78 : 0<br>8  0x100800100  0.971534 : 0<br>9  0x100800128  -0.971534 : 0<br>10  0x100800150  1.19392 : 0<br>11  0x100800170  -2.16546 : 0<br>12  0x100800198  -3.08439 : 0<p>MIDDLE STACK<br>STACK, size=13<br>0  0x100800000  -2.7 : 0.422406<br>1  0x100800018  1.9 : -0.422406<br>2  0x100800030  3.3 : 0.285778<br>3  0x100800048  0 : 1<br>4  0x100800060  -4.6 : 0.422406<br>5  0x100800088  21.16 : -0.0459137<br>6  0x1008000b0  10.89 : 0.0892134<br>7  0x1008000d8  21.78 : 0.0446067<br>8  0x100800100  0.971534 : -1<br>9  0x100800128  -0.971534 : 1<br>10  0x100800150  1.19392 : -1<br>11  0x100800170  -2.16546 : 1<br>12  0x100800198  -3.08439 : 1<p>So somehow the very first step is getting<br>poluted, but AFTER the gradient starts<br>propagating.  Very curious.<p>- Bob<br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
